-- title:
--   Theorem C.1 — diminishing-step stationarity criterion
-- statement:
--   Suppose Assumption 3.1 holds, $J\ge1$ is finite and $\varepsilon\ge0$ is fixed, and the deterministic sequences satisfy $\eta_t>0$, $\beta_t\in[0,1)$, $\theta_t\in[0,1]$ ($t\ge1$), with the step sizes obeying (C.3):
--
--   $$
--   \sum_{t=1}^\infty\eta_t=\infty,\qquad\sum_{t=1}^\infty\eta_t^2<\infty .
--   $$
--
--   Let $W_t,M_t$ be generated by the Muon recursion (3.1)–(3.3) from deterministic $W_1,M_0$, with $g_t=\nabla F(W_t)$ and $r_t=N_t-g_t$.
--
--   1. Along a deterministic trajectory (any perturbation sequence $\zeta_t$), if $\sum_{t\ge1}\eta_t\|r_t\|<\infty$ (C.4), then $\|g_t\|\to0$.
--   2. For random iterates (random perturbations $\zeta_t$ on a probability space), if
--
--   $$
--   \sum_{t=1}^\infty\eta_t\,\mathbb E\|r_t\|<\infty, \tag{C.5}
--   $$
--
--   then $\|g_t\|\to0$ almost surely and $\mathbb E\|g_t\|^2\to0$.
--
--   The criterion reduces last-iterate stationarity of Muon to a single weighted summability condition on the input discrepancy $r_t$, independently of how $N_t$ is formed.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Expectations of nonnegative quantities are lower Lebesgue integrals with values in $[0,\infty]$; hence (C.5) asserts that every $\mathbb E\|r_t\|$ is finite with a finite weighted sum, and $\mathbb E\|g_t\|^2\to0$ cannot hold through a junk value of a non-integrable function.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--
--   - reading: “for random iterates” → the perturbations ζ_t are measurable maps on a probability space and the iterates are the recursion applied pathwise; reason: random iterates are random variables; ∇F is continuous and Φ_ε is Borel, so the iterates are then measurable
--   - encoding: E‖r_t‖ and E‖g_t‖² as expectations; ∑ η_t = ∞ → lower Lebesgue integrals in [0, ∞]; (C.5) as a [0, ∞]-valued sum ≠ ∞; partial sums of η_t tend to +∞; reason: the quantities are nonnegative, so the extended-valued expectation is the source's and no integrability hypothesis is hidden
--   - encoding: real m×n matrices with Frobenius norm ‖X‖_F and inner product tr(XᵀY) → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin m × Fin n), read as a matrix through toMat for the products of (3.4); reason: the Euclidean norm and inner product on this type are exactly the Frobenius ones (checked in the sanity file); same instances
-- source:
--   Ping Li and Vincent Y. F. Tan, Last-Iterate Stationarity of Muon with Finitely Many Newton-Schulz Iterations, STOC 2027 submission #110 preprint (2026), source.pdf SHA-256 5362e7185a9ddcba39d1a70da110a8b04f1d179ad818e6d5d0ec73bf29586372, p.21, Theorem C.1, (C.4), (C.5); proof p.23; https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-1/110.pdf

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_MuonLastIterate110_Stochastic_Muon

open Filter Topology MeasureTheory
open scoped ENNReal

namespace MuonLastIterate110.Stochastic

/-- Theorem C.1 (Diminishing-step stationarity criterion), p.21. Suppose Assumption 3.1 holds,
`J ≥ 1` and `ε ≥ 0` are fixed, the deterministic sequences satisfy `η_t > 0`, `β_t ∈ [0,1)`,
`θ_t ∈ [0,1]` (`t ≥ 1`), and the steps satisfy (C.3): `∑ η_t = ∞`, `∑ η_t² < ∞`.
1. Deterministic trajectory: for every perturbation sequence `ζ` driving (3.1)–(3.3), if
   `∑_{t ≥ 1} η_t ‖r_t‖ < ∞` (C.4), then `‖g_t‖ → 0`.
2. Random iterates: if the perturbations `ζ_t` are random variables on a probability space and
   `∑_{t ≥ 1} η_t E‖r_t‖ < ∞` (C.5), then `‖g_t‖ → 0` almost surely and `E‖g_t‖² → 0`.
Expectations are lower Lebesgue integrals in `[0, ∞]`, so (C.5) asserts finiteness of every term
and `E‖g_t‖² → 0` cannot hold through a junk value. -/
theorem theorem_c_1 {m n : ℕ} (S : Muon m n) (L Finf : ℝ) (hF : Assumption31 S.F L Finf)
    (hS : S.Admissible)
    (hdiv : Tendsto (fun T : ℕ => ∑ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, S.η t) atTop atTop)
    (hsq : Summable (fun t : ℕ => S.η (t + 1) ^ 2)) :
    (∀ ζ : ℕ → Mat m n,
        Summable (fun t : ℕ => S.η (t + 1) * ‖S.r ζ (t + 1)‖) →
        Tendsto (fun t => ‖S.g ζ t‖) atTop (𝓝 0)) ∧
    (∀ {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (μ : Measure Ω) [IsProbabilityMeasure μ]
        (ζ : ℕ → Ω → Mat m n), (∀ t, Measurable (ζ t)) →
        (∑' t : ℕ, ENNReal.ofReal (S.η (t + 1)) *
            ∫⁻ ω, ‖S.r (fun s => ζ s ω) (t + 1)‖ₑ ∂μ) ≠ ∞ →
        (∀ᵐ ω ∂μ, Tendsto (fun t => ‖S.g (fun s => ζ s ω) t‖) atTop (𝓝 0)) ∧
        Tendsto (fun t => ∫⁻ ω, ENNReal.ofReal (‖S.g (fun s => ζ s ω) t‖ ^ 2) ∂μ)
          atTop (𝓝 0)) := by sorry

end MuonLastIterate110.Stochastic
